Points well made.  I am a programmer myself (not on devteam), and know
that this hellblade would be hell to implement.  I certainly wouldn't
want to see it in this form -- this is a rough draft for discussion
only.  Certainly there are number of features that would need to be
trimmed out.  But here are the basic points I am aiming at:

1. It has to be an evil intelligent weapon.
2. It has to be a temptation weapon -- that is, it has immediate
obvious benefits and not-so-obvious long-term drawbacks.
3. In order to make it tempting, it has to be more than a piece of junk
like e.g. Cleaver. Otherwise people will just throw it away.
4. And if it's going to have some obvious benefits, it has to have a
real kick-in-the-teeth malevolent (but subtle) effect, otherwise people
will just use the weapon and endure the curse.

-- As a quest artifact there is a point: The Quest Leader is lawful --
probably a Tokugawa, since the Tokugawas were the Shoguns.   It would
make since that he would fear the Quest Nemesis laying his hands on an
accursed blade which could be used to end the reign of the Shogun.

But if so, the quest will not be to RECOVER the artifact -- it will be
to DESTROY the artifact.  The Tokugawa had no interest in having these
things around -- they brought a curse on the Tokugawa merely by
existing. To them, a Muramasa blade is wholly evil, like the Ring in
Lord of the Rings.

As such, the person who recovers the blade should have the following
choices:

1.  Destroy the weapon, and be rewarded for it (it had better be a big
reward, as we're talking about voluntarily depriving ourselves of a
major artifact).

2.  Secretly keep the weapon, while lying to the quest leader that it
has been destroyed.  This is where the temptation aspect comes in.

3.  Kill the Quest Leader with the Muramasa.  This is what the Muramasa
is DESIGNED for.  It has been forged for one purpose alone: the death
of the Tokugawa.  Allowing it to fulfill the one goal of it's existence
should make the Chaotic Powers VERY happy and the Lawful Powers VERY
upset.    It should, at the very least, put one's alignment in serious
jeopardy.

------------
